WEBVTT

00:00:01.807 --> 00:00:10.565
Enquiries & Leads
From a website enquiry to a new client with a loan application — routed, scored and timed automatically.

00:00:10.566 --> 00:00:15.511
A prospect calls Priya about a personal loan
She emails the website enquiry form instead of typing the details in herself

00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:22.847
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Relationship manager — first point of contact

00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:28.609
Tools ▸ Web forms lists every form published on the website
Email it, copy the link, or open it — answers become CRM records

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:37.293
Client email, name, language and a personal note
Personal Loan is already chosen for her

00:00:37.293 --> 00:00:42.464
The client gets a short email with a button that opens the form
The email is recorded under Email logs

00:00:42.464 --> 00:00:45.335
Aditi opens the link from the email
Same form as on the website — no account needed

00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:50.679
She gives the amount but leaves the tenure empty
Not every client knows it yet — we will see why it matters

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:58.271
Next page: contact details and consent to be contacted

00:00:58.271 --> 00:01:02.183
She gets a reference number straight away
And an acknowledgement email in her language

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:06.941
Routing gave it to Yash Bholah in the Lending team
Personal loans go to the loans executives in turn

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:13.963
Sign in as Yash Bholah — Loans Executive
Loans executive — owns the new enquiry

00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:18.864
Yash finds it in the New column of the enquiry funnel
New → Contacted → Qualified → Converted, or Nurture / Disqualified

00:01:18.864 --> 00:01:24.017
Everything the client typed is on the record
Channel: website form · consent captured with its date and wording

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:31.134
Calculated for her: entity and queue, lead score and grade, indicative rate
Score uses amount, contact details, consent and channel — grade A to F

00:01:31.134 --> 00:01:36.732
The speed-to-lead clock started too: first contact within 4 business hours
Tools ▸ SLA Board shows it with the time remaining

00:01:36.732 --> 00:01:43.797
After calling Aditi, Yash drags the card to Contacted
That stops the first-response clock

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:52.937
Need confirmed: on to Qualified
Qualified needs an email and a product — both are there

00:01:55.349 --> 00:02:01.483
Next: convert it
A loan enquiry needs an amount and a tenure — they start the loan application

00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:08.352
Blocked: the card goes back and the message says what is missing
"Open record to complete" goes straight to the form

00:02:08.352 --> 00:02:13.262
Add the tenure Aditi gave on the phone: 60 months

00:02:13.262 --> 00:02:17.947
Now the move to Converted goes through

00:02:20.356 --> 00:02:27.113
Converting runs the onboarding automatically
Client record · entity relationship · KYC case · consent · loan application

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:30.421
The enquiry now points to the new client record
Converted to party

00:02:30.421 --> 00:02:38.185
Related: the loan application, started at Pre-qualified with amount and tenure
The loans team continues there (see the Retail Lending tutorial)

00:02:38.185 --> 00:02:54.296
The new client: relationship with the lending entity, KYC case and marketing consent
Clients ▸ the client record ▸ Related

00:02:54.296 --> 00:02:57.801
Yash shares a personal link with another prospect
Web forms ▸ Talk to: the enquiry comes straight back, skipping routing

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:03.369
Copied — pasted into a WhatsApp message to Yannick

00:03:03.369 --> 00:03:20.402
The form says "You'll speak with Yash Bholah"

00:03:20.402 --> 00:03:28.161
Sign in as Yash Bholah — Loans Executive
Back in the CRM

00:03:28.161 --> 00:03:37.039
After the call: no income yet, so not eligible
Disqualified needs a reason — the move is refused without one

00:03:37.039 --> 00:03:49.256
The form opens with the missing field on top
Reason: Not eligible

00:03:54.247 --> 00:03:58.126
Disqualification reasons feed the Lead Funnel dashboard
So marketing sees why leads are lost

00:03:58.126 --> 00:04:19.246
Aditi also wants to invest — a job for Wealth Management
Referrals pass a client from one Genesis entity to another, with credit to the referrer

00:04:19.246 --> 00:04:24.710
It goes straight to the receiving RM named on it — Priya in Wealth
She has one business day to accept it (referral SLA)

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:31.539
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Wealth RM receiving the referral

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:36.166
The referral is waiting in her Submitted column
Accepting it stops the one-day clock; Won or Lost records the outcome

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:54.273
For wealth enquiries Priya uses the guided wizard
Enquiries ▸ Wealth enquiry — qualify: contact, then needs

00:04:54.273 --> 00:05:09.283
Investable assets and horizon — what the wealth team needs to qualify

00:05:09.283 --> 00:05:15.307
Aditi is recognised as an existing client — no duplicate will be created
Existing client plus a referral: the lead score jumps to grade A

00:05:15.307 --> 00:05:21.327
Shalini, Head of Business Development, watches the top of the funnel
Calculator sessions: anonymous loan-calculator visits from the website

00:05:21.327 --> 00:05:29.785
Sign in as Shalini Ramtohul — Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships
Head of BD & Strategic Partnerships

00:05:29.785 --> 00:05:36.377
Product, amount and indicative instalment each visitor looked at
Converted shows whether the visitor later left details as an enquiry

00:05:36.377 --> 00:05:41.304
Newsletter sign-ups and call-back requests land here too
A call-back request creates an enquiry for the right team automatically

00:05:41.304 --> 00:05:47.870
Enquiries & Leads
